# The working tree is LF on every machine, including Windows.
#
# `build.mjs` writes LF, and it compares the generated language selector and
# hreflang set against what is already in the English pages. A checkout that
# converted those pages to CRLF made every one of those comparisons fail, and
# would have written pages with CRLF around the translated blocks and LF inside
# them. The build now normalises what it reads, so this is belt as well as
# braces — but a repository whose files are one thing in git and another on
# disk has a whole category of problem available to it, and this closes it.
* text=auto eol=lf
